\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Axis-aligned pipeline-sensitivity diagnostic and observed-effect scale. (A--B) Brain and PBMC ladders; lines show the mean across 30 independent noise replicates, ribbons the replicate range, and diamonds the subdivided low-$\alpha $ points. (C) Observed effects located on the injection curves. (D) $\alpha $-equivalents of the six supported positive rows relative to the smallest probed nonzero fraction; the negative brain attention row has no positive $\alpha $-equivalent. This is not a confidence interval, power curve, MDE, or exclusion analysis.}}{14}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sensitivity}{{9}{14}{Axis-aligned pipeline-sensitivity diagnostic and observed-effect scale. (A--B) Brain and PBMC ladders; lines show the mean across 30 independent noise replicates, ribbons the replicate range, and diamonds the subdivided low-$\alpha $ points. (C) Observed effects located on the injection curves. (D) $\alpha $-equivalents of the six supported positive rows relative to the smallest probed nonzero fraction; the negative brain attention row has no positive $\alpha $-equivalent. This is not a confidence interval, power curve, MDE, or exclusion analysis}{figure.caption.12}{}}
